# WebinoDashboard — Core Rules

## Stack (mandatory)

- **Backend:** Laravel (latest stable). API-first only.
- **Frontend:** Next.js App Router + official [shadcn/ui](https://ui.shadcn.com/).
- **Deploy:** Dockerized microservices — separate `frontend` and `backend` containers (`docker-compose.aapanel.yml`). Never merge them into one runtime image for production.

## Quality bar

- No placeholders, stubs, “TODO UI”, or fake data in shipped paths.
- Auth must be complete: no gaps in cookie/session/Sanctum, middleware gates, or setup redirects.
- No hard-coded user-facing strings (UI, errors, nav, empty states) — use i18n keys.
- Every visible site/admin setting (logo, colors, accent, copy, fonts) must be editable from the dashboard. Never ship a front-end value the tenant cannot change.

## Architecture

- Modular: every feature and every third-party integration lives inside its own module/submodule (manifest + backend routes + frontend pages).
- Shared capabilities (payments, cart, catalog) belong in **commerce**; verticals (cafe, shop) only customize — they do not reimplement gateways.
- Public and admin UIs are **SSR**. Target first meaningful paint / LCP under **1 second** on a typical VPS path (cache public GETs, avoid client waterfalls).
- Mobile-first and responsive for all breakpoints (sm/md/lg/xl). Do not ship desktop-only layouts.

## Pages (official shadcn blocks)

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add login-04
npx shadcn@latest add sidebar-07
```

Never hand-draw login or sidebar “inspired by” shadcn. Always add from the official CLI and import the generated components.

## Themes

- New vertical UI ships as a **starter** theme (`cafe-starter`, `ecommerce-starter` / shop starter, …), not only `*-default`.
- Theme chrome + module pages must consume branding/settings from the API.

## Forbidden

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — hard-coded copy / placeholder
<button>ثبت نام</button>
<div>Coming soon</div>

// ✅ GOOD — translation key + real implementation
<button>{t("auth.register")}</button>
```
